        // Read the ADVERSARIAL COUNTERPARTY rule: if the difference only manifests through the behaviour of an external party (like a failing callee), we must deploy a helper. Here the difference is about a require that always fails, so it's not about an external party. The difference is in the airdrop method itself. So no adversarial helper required. We can directly test the property.
